# Build output: all of it is regenerable, none of it belongs in a commit.
# The one native binary that IS tracked is the staged engine under
# src/Andzip.Native/runtimes/<rid>/native/ -- without it, "dotnet build" needs the
# C++ toolchain and CI's managed jobs cannot run at all. See step 1 of the build
# section in README.md.
build/
dist/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/

# Visual Studio per-user state. It also holds the chosen startup project, which is
# why a stale copy can make F5 fail even after the solution is fixed.
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# Test/coverage output
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage

# Editor scratch
*.log
*.tmp

# Materialised by cmake/codecs.cmake at configure time (only when
# -DANDZIP_EXTRA_CODECS=ON) from third_party/codecs/xxhash/xxhash.h, because
# zstd's zstd_internal.h includes "../hashes/xxhash.h". Committing it would put a
# second copy of that header in the tree, which is exactly what we avoided.
native/third_party/7zip/C/hashes/
